1200
00:57:31.020 --> 00:57:34.340
And I thought, that's not good.

1201
00:57:34.900 --> 00:57:36.580
You should have used some tongs.

1202
00:57:36.780 --> 00:57:37.560
Some tongs.

1203
00:57:37.580 --> 00:57:38.860
He just handed to me with his hands.

1204
00:57:38.960 --> 00:57:42.340
And so I improvised that line and it stayed in and it makes me laugh.

1205
00:57:42.340 --> 00:57:44.200
Of course, she goes ahead and eats it.

1206
00:57:44.320 --> 00:57:45.860
So I guess she's not too concerned.

1207
00:57:46.260 --> 00:57:49.760
But it's clearly she's just like not having a good time.

1208
00:57:49.940 --> 00:57:53.820
And she's a little like grossed out because she's seeing a lot of feet.

1209
00:57:54.180 --> 00:57:56.900
And now a guy just handed her bread with his hands.

1210
00:57:57.040 --> 00:57:57.540
A stranger.

1211
00:57:57.820 --> 00:58:02.440
Well, in the script, it says that you take a bite and say, ugh, garlic.

1212
00:58:02.440 --> 00:58:05.880
Like, we had some fan questions about the foods.

1213
00:58:06.120 --> 00:58:11.020
Stacey and Rutt V both wrote in to say, was any of that delicious looking buffet food real?

1214
00:58:11.420 --> 00:58:14.760
Did you get to sample some of the cuisine while filming this episode?

1215
00:58:14.980 --> 00:58:16.820
Guys, it was all real food.

1216
00:58:17.860 --> 00:58:18.980
It was all real.

1217
00:58:19.160 --> 00:58:20.000
It was all delicious.

1218
00:58:20.360 --> 00:58:26.520
Kent told me we hired a specialty food stylist to create the food, that it was authentically prepared.

1219
00:58:26.520 --> 00:58:30.140
And we had it all three days of filming and we got to eat it.

1220
00:58:30.260 --> 00:58:32.260
And I remember that it was delicious.

1221
00:58:32.620 --> 00:58:33.320
It was delicious.

1222
00:58:33.340 --> 00:58:36.140
I only got to eat the naan, but it was very good naan.

1223
00:58:36.860 --> 00:58:38.780
Oh, I ate between takes.

1224
00:58:39.320 --> 00:58:40.360
I just ate it.

1225
00:58:40.680 --> 00:58:43.000
You don't even see Pam eating it on screen.

1226
00:58:43.000 --> 00:58:44.440
I was like, I will eat this.

1227
00:58:44.680 --> 00:58:50.340
Well, now we come to one of the moments in this episode that is one of my favorites, Angela.

1228
00:58:50.340 --> 00:58:54.240
This is when Ryan meets Kelly's giggly sisters.

1229
00:58:54.720 --> 00:58:54.900
Yeah.

1230
00:58:55.440 --> 00:58:57.540
It's so, so cute.

1231
00:58:57.720 --> 00:59:02.740
We got some fan questions from Lindsay, Bridget, and Dan, who all want to know,

1232
00:59:02.900 --> 00:59:07.060
do you know what Kelly's sister is saying when they're talking to Ryan?

1233
00:59:07.240 --> 00:59:09.280
They're saying something about Zach Braff.

1234
00:59:09.540 --> 00:59:11.820
Okay, here's what the three little girls say.

1235
00:59:12.060 --> 00:59:14.940
They say, Kelly likes Zach Braff.

1236
00:59:15.660 --> 00:59:17.780
That's what they're saying in Hindi.

1237
00:59:17.880 --> 00:59:19.300
And they're sort of like teasing him.

1238
00:59:19.300 --> 00:59:21.060
They were so cute.

1239
00:59:21.240 --> 00:59:25.720
And they were played by Tanvir Atwal, Ananya Keper, and Jaysha Patel.

1240
00:59:25.920 --> 00:59:32.200
Well, the little girl who plays Kelly's sister that says the Zach Braff line, that's Jaysha.

1241
00:59:32.460 --> 00:59:37.940
I found her on Instagram, and I reached out to her to ask her about what it was like to be on the show.

1242
00:59:37.940 --> 00:59:39.040
And she wrote back.

1243
00:59:39.040 --> 00:59:40.360
I can't wait to share.

1244
00:59:40.580 --> 00:59:42.960
She must be like a grown lady now.

1245
00:59:43.160 --> 00:59:44.960
She is a grown woman now.

1246
00:59:44.960 --> 00:59:48.340
She told me she was 13 years old when she shot this episode.

1247
00:59:48.340 --> 00:59:51.580
She said she had not really heard about the show.

1248
00:59:51.880 --> 00:59:54.820
She was still watching Disney Channel, she said.

1249
00:59:54.980 --> 01:00:06.300
But she said her dad took her to the audition, and she remembers walking into the casting office and just seeing tons of other kids who were all there for the same role.

1250
01:00:06.300 --> 01:00:10.160
And she said the audition was just her saying that one line in Hindi.

1251
01:00:10.520 --> 01:00:12.620
And she said she didn't speak any Hindi.

1252
01:00:12.820 --> 01:00:18.000
So her dad told her how to say it about five seconds before she went into the audition room.

1253
01:00:18.100 --> 01:00:19.540
And then she got the part.

1254
01:00:19.540 --> 01:00:22.540
So she said she was so excited.

1255
01:00:22.540 --> 01:00:26.580
And I asked her what it was like to be on set, if she had any memories.

1256
01:00:26.580 --> 01:00:28.840
And she sent back the sweetest message.

1257
01:00:28.840 --> 01:00:30.520
So we're going to play it for you now.

1258
01:00:31.160 --> 01:00:36.040
I remember Rainn Wilson walking up to me and shoving a lightsaber in my hand and yelling,

1259
01:00:36.180 --> 01:00:37.100
Lightsaber war!

1260
01:00:37.100 --> 01:00:42.220
I also remember getting to know Mindy Kaling and BJ Novak, who were so sweet to me.

1261
01:00:42.740 --> 01:00:49.920
Meeting Mindy Kaling really meant a lot to me growing up because I didn't really see many Indian actresses in the entertainment industry at that time.

1262
01:00:49.980 --> 01:00:55.580
And I love what Mindy has done with her platform, and she is still a huge inspiration for me till this day.

1263
01:00:55.800 --> 01:01:00.200
I also remember all of the delicious Indian food on set and getting to dance all day.

1264
01:01:00.400 --> 01:01:04.280
And I remember being so happy that I had the chance to wear my Indian clothes.

1265
01:01:04.740 --> 01:01:05.960
Isn't that so sweet?

1266
01:01:05.960 --> 01:01:07.080
That is wonderful.

1267
01:01:07.500 --> 01:01:12.580
As I listened to it, I was just smiling so big because everything about that message is lovely.

1268
01:01:12.740 --> 01:01:13.840
I love all of her memories.

1269
01:01:14.000 --> 01:01:17.460
She's absolutely right about Mindy and what Mindy has done.

1270
01:01:17.540 --> 01:01:20.460
And she's such an inspiration to so many people.

1271
01:01:21.520 --> 01:01:22.060
Yes.

1272
01:01:22.420 --> 01:01:22.800
Yeah.

1273
01:01:23.280 --> 01:01:32.660
She told me after the episode aired, she had classmates and family members reaching out that they had recorded it and taking pictures of her name in the credits.

1274
01:01:34.200 --> 01:01:35.960
So that was when she was 13.

1275
01:01:35.960 --> 01:01:37.320
She really wanted to be an actress.

1276
01:01:37.540 --> 01:01:41.980
She said when she was 15, she decided she wanted to go into journalism.

1277
01:01:41.980 --> 01:01:47.220
And now, Jayshia is the morning news reporter at NBC15 in Mobile, Alabama.

1278
01:01:47.760 --> 01:01:54.220
She told me she has to go to bed at 4 o'clock in the afternoon because she has to be in the studio at 3.30 in the morning.

1279
01:01:54.220 --> 01:02:01.840
I have always heard that about these morning anchors on the East Coast, that they have to get up so early.

1280
01:02:02.140 --> 01:02:03.840
That's amazing, though, Jayshia.

1281
01:02:04.080 --> 01:02:05.200
That is so cool.

1282
01:02:05.600 --> 01:02:06.600
Isn't that so cool?

1283
01:02:06.740 --> 01:02:13.520
She said all her co-workers know about her appearance on The Office and that fans will mention to her because she's Indian.

1284
01:02:13.960 --> 01:02:19.740
They'll mention the Diwali episode, and then she always, like, blows their mind when she says, oh, no, I was in it.

1285
01:02:20.120 --> 01:02:21.700
So I thought that was so sweet.

1286
01:02:21.980 --> 01:02:22.660
I was in it.

1287
01:02:22.720 --> 01:02:25.040
I say a line that offends Ryan the Temp.

1288
01:02:26.100 --> 01:02:26.900
Yes, exactly.

1289
01:02:27.240 --> 01:02:30.420
Except he doesn't quite know he's being the butt of a joke.

1290
01:02:30.680 --> 01:02:30.860
Right.

1291
01:02:30.860 --> 01:02:36.460
But she said being on The Office was one of her most memorable moments of her childhood.

1292
01:02:36.740 --> 01:02:41.580
I also love that, you know, I'm sure Rain improvised going up to her with that lightsaber.

1293
01:02:41.860 --> 01:02:45.920
There's a bunch of deleted scenes where he's fighting with kids with lightsabers.

1294
01:02:47.160 --> 01:02:48.520
And it didn't make it in.

1295
01:02:48.620 --> 01:02:53.300
But he, Rain looked very much in his element, like that's how he bonds with children.

1296
01:02:54.000 --> 01:02:54.340
Yes.

1297
01:02:54.660 --> 01:02:58.220
Angela, should we check in on those folks at Stanford, see how they're doing?

1298
01:02:58.220 --> 01:03:00.480
You mean the folks drinking Jägermeister?

1299
01:03:00.800 --> 01:03:01.020
Yeah.

1300
01:03:01.280 --> 01:03:01.980
How are they?

1301
01:03:02.280 --> 01:03:04.500
And Angela, did you see what they ordered for dinner?

1302
01:03:04.640 --> 01:03:06.440
Oh, Jenna, you and I know firsthand.

1303
01:03:07.280 --> 01:03:11.620
You do not drink a lot of alcohol and only eat sushi.

1304
01:03:12.040 --> 01:03:13.820
Now, Angela, why do we know that firsthand?

1305
01:03:13.820 --> 01:03:17.720
We know that because at the Golden Globes, was it the Golden Globes, Jenna?

1306
01:03:18.780 --> 01:03:22.520
Oh, lady, I was thinking of my bachelorette party that you planned for me.

1307
01:03:22.560 --> 01:03:24.720
Oh, well, there was the Golden Globes, but the bachelorette?

1308
01:03:24.920 --> 01:03:27.740
Wait, have we repeated this mistake multiple times?

1309
01:03:27.740 --> 01:03:30.260
Except the second time, I did better.

1310
01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:32.820
The first time, it did not work out well for me.

1311
01:03:32.940 --> 01:03:39.520
The second time, if memory serves, sorry to say this on here, but it hit your sister pretty hard.

1312
01:03:40.440 --> 01:03:41.000
Yeah.

1313
01:03:41.480 --> 01:03:46.040
Guys, Angela planned a bachelorette party for me when I was getting married to Lee,

1314
01:03:46.080 --> 01:03:49.180
and she took us all out for a sushi dinner.

1315
01:03:49.400 --> 01:03:55.380
It was a fancy schmancy sushi place in Beverly Hills that I'd never eaten at,

1316
01:03:55.380 --> 01:03:56.640
that I'd only dreamed of.

1317
01:03:56.800 --> 01:03:59.840
And I was like, can we go there for my bachelorette?

1318
01:03:59.960 --> 01:04:01.780
They were thrilled to have us.

1319
01:04:01.940 --> 01:04:02.840
It was so cute.

1320
01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:04.840
All of the ladies from the office were there.

1321
01:04:05.060 --> 01:04:06.780
All of my other friends were there.

1322
01:04:06.940 --> 01:04:11.640
And afterwards, you took us to a dance club.

1323
01:04:11.940 --> 01:04:12.680
Hold up, lady.

1324
01:04:12.960 --> 01:04:14.360
We're going to get this right.

1325
01:04:14.640 --> 01:04:17.480
First of all, the sushi place was your idea.

1326
01:04:17.480 --> 01:04:21.740
And then after the sushi place, you guys, I got cupcakes with like her face on it.

1327
01:04:21.840 --> 01:04:22.460
It was so cute.

1328
01:04:22.680 --> 01:04:25.840
We had lots of free drinks sent over.

1329
01:04:25.960 --> 01:04:29.340
The restaurant was very kind and lots of great sushi.

1330
01:04:30.020 --> 01:04:35.420
And then after the dinner, I was like, well, thank you guys.

1331
01:04:35.600 --> 01:04:36.820
And Jenna was like, what's next?

1332
01:04:37.060 --> 01:04:38.840
And I was like, uh, what?

1333
01:04:40.160 --> 01:04:40.860
Wait, what?

1334
01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:41.340
Do you not?

1335
01:04:41.540 --> 01:04:42.320
Is this true?

1336
01:04:42.620 --> 01:04:43.800
I do not remember this.

1337
01:04:43.800 --> 01:04:44.500
No.

1338
01:04:44.800 --> 01:04:47.040
Lady, all I had planned was the dinner.

1339
01:04:47.280 --> 01:04:49.240
I didn't plan anything after.

1340
01:04:49.440 --> 01:04:51.580
Is this the first time you're ever hearing of this?

1341
01:04:52.440 --> 01:04:52.920
Yes.

1342
01:04:54.520 --> 01:04:58.880
This is putting the dance club into perspective now.

1343
01:04:59.040 --> 01:05:01.480
Because I thought at the time it was an odd choice.

1344
01:05:02.160 --> 01:05:05.060
Because we've never in a million years gone clubbing.

1345
01:05:05.260 --> 01:05:08.200
And now we were suddenly clubbing for my bachelorette.

1346
01:05:08.280 --> 01:05:09.780
But I was like, this is great.

1347
01:05:09.940 --> 01:05:10.800
What a fun idea.

1348
01:05:11.100 --> 01:05:12.520
I should say, you guys, we had a car.

1349
01:05:12.520 --> 01:05:15.780
I got one of the big limos, you know, that we could all pile in.

1350
01:05:15.880 --> 01:05:20.800
And I called a friend of mine who was like, always kind of like, got, you know, you have

1351
01:05:20.800 --> 01:05:22.320
that one friend that's like, I got to hook up.

1352
01:05:22.460 --> 01:05:23.060
I got to hook up.

1353
01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:24.320
Yeah.

1354
01:05:24.480 --> 01:05:25.040
I'm in the know.

1355
01:05:25.360 --> 01:05:26.540
I called my friend Tess.

1356
01:05:26.700 --> 01:05:30.780
And I was like, Tess, um, I, I, Jenna wants to go dancing.

1357
01:05:30.860 --> 01:05:32.700
I were in Beverly Hills.

1358
01:05:32.820 --> 01:05:33.200
What do I do?

1359
01:05:33.300 --> 01:05:33.740
What do I do?

1360
01:05:33.840 --> 01:05:34.880
And she was like, I'm on it.

1361
01:05:35.260 --> 01:05:36.480
Give me like five, 10 minutes.

1362
01:05:36.620 --> 01:05:37.100
I said, okay.

1363
01:05:38.040 --> 01:05:39.600
So we kind of hung out a little bit.

1364
01:05:39.600 --> 01:05:42.060
And I was like, um, I'm sorting out some stuff, guys.

1365
01:05:42.280 --> 01:05:45.060
I do remember hanging out on the sidewalk outside.

1366
01:05:45.320 --> 01:05:45.660
Yes.

1367
01:05:45.780 --> 01:05:49.960
It's because I didn't have a plan because the restaurant I had planned for was fancy sushi.

1368
01:05:50.740 --> 01:05:53.480
And our evening would have been over at like 10 o'clock.

1369
01:05:53.860 --> 01:05:54.100
Yeah.

1370
01:05:54.520 --> 01:05:59.900
Anyway, I get a call from Tess and she goes, all right, Angela's pretty last minute.

1371
01:06:00.160 --> 01:06:02.920
It's like, you know, a Thursday night in Beverly Hills.

1372
01:06:02.920 --> 01:06:04.840
So I did get you in this one club.

1373
01:06:05.020 --> 01:06:09.080
I know this guy, he's got a booth for you and they're going to give you drink service.

1374
01:06:09.320 --> 01:06:11.440
It's kind of a random club, but it'll be fun.

1375
01:06:11.540 --> 01:06:12.540
You guys can dance.

1376
01:06:13.040 --> 01:06:17.160
Angela, it's the only time I've ever experienced bottle service.

1377
01:06:17.740 --> 01:06:23.920
Bottle service is where you like, they bring you just bottles of alcohol and then mixers

1378
01:06:23.920 --> 01:06:28.240
and like little cut limes to your table and you make your drink.

1379
01:06:28.560 --> 01:06:31.880
Also, when they walk it over, everyone starts doing, at least for us,

1380
01:06:31.880 --> 01:06:35.360
I think this was the norm because I would see different people get bottle service and it was

1381
01:06:35.360 --> 01:06:39.900
like, and they shut off like confetti in the air.

1382
01:06:40.020 --> 01:06:40.980
It was so weird.

1383
01:06:41.200 --> 01:06:42.320
It was so bizarre.

1384
01:06:42.620 --> 01:06:44.880
They had, it was crazy dancing.

1385
01:06:45.060 --> 01:06:49.740
I remember we got in trouble because we were dancing on top of the couches and we got reprimanded

1386
01:06:49.740 --> 01:06:50.240
for that.

1387
01:06:50.960 --> 01:07:00.260
But guys, on our stomachs of sushi mixed with bottle service, long story short, at the end

1388
01:07:00.260 --> 01:07:05.800
of the night, as the limo is dropping everyone off, my sister puked in Ellie Kemper's bushes.

1389
01:07:07.720 --> 01:07:09.580
I puked when I got home.

1390
01:07:09.780 --> 01:07:10.980
It was in my hair.

1391
01:07:11.180 --> 01:07:12.280
I slept in it.

1392
01:07:12.760 --> 01:07:14.480
It was an epic night.

1393
01:07:14.820 --> 01:07:18.700
But that's what you get when you mix sushi and a lot of booze.

1394
01:07:18.820 --> 01:07:21.400
And that is what is in store for these guys in Stanford.

1395
01:07:21.400 --> 01:07:26.300
Yeah, as Jenna and I rewatched this episode, I texted her and I was like, oh, lady, alcohol

1396
01:07:26.300 --> 01:07:26.980
and sushi.

1397
01:07:27.840 --> 01:07:29.080
It's so true.

1398
01:07:29.080 --> 01:07:31.060
It is so true.

1399
01:07:31.860 --> 01:07:33.500
Should we go back to Diwali?

1400
01:07:33.840 --> 01:07:37.780
Because Roy has arrived and he is watching Pam dance and have fun.

1401
01:07:38.340 --> 01:07:41.600
And I have a full Mindy catch for you right here.

1402
01:07:41.600 --> 01:07:44.240
And we've got a sting for it and everything.

1403
01:07:47.550 --> 01:07:48.610
There you go.

1404
01:07:48.830 --> 01:07:50.290
It's a full Mindy catch.

1405
01:07:50.830 --> 01:07:58.070
Mira During wrote in to say, at the Diwali party when Roy walks in, Beyonce's crazy in love

1406
01:07:58.070 --> 01:07:59.670
is playing in the background.

1407
01:07:59.950 --> 01:08:02.830
And Angela, this was a note in the script.

1408
01:08:03.130 --> 01:08:08.810
Mindy wrote in what song would be playing when Roy walks in and that it would be a Beyonce

1409
01:08:08.810 --> 01:08:09.310
song.

1410
01:08:09.490 --> 01:08:12.750
So I think this is a full, full Mindy.

1411
01:08:12.750 --> 01:08:13.830
I love it.

1412
01:08:13.910 --> 01:08:15.890
It's a very subtle, full Mindy.

1413
01:08:16.090 --> 01:08:20.810
It's like full Mindy when you don't even see Mindy, but her presence is still there.

1414
01:08:21.210 --> 01:08:21.730
Exactly.

1415
01:08:22.170 --> 01:08:27.670
And, you know, my dance partner, we talked about this in the interview with Mindy, my

1416
01:08:27.670 --> 01:08:28.870
dance partner, Valli.

1417
01:08:29.310 --> 01:08:33.870
OK, he was well known by the writers because he was a writer on My Name is Earl at the time.

1418
01:08:34.330 --> 01:08:40.390
And he went on to write on 30 Rock and was one of the executive producers of Modern Family.

1419
01:08:40.550 --> 01:08:41.410
Oh, my gosh.

1420
01:08:41.410 --> 01:08:41.750
Oh, my gosh.

1421
01:08:42.430 --> 01:08:43.030
I know.

1422
01:08:43.250 --> 01:08:45.650
Well, Mindy did say, guys, he wasn't an actor.

1423
01:08:45.790 --> 01:08:46.990
He was like a friend of ours.

1424
01:08:48.550 --> 01:08:49.450
That's so wild.

1425
01:08:49.630 --> 01:08:52.990
Well, can I ask you a little bit about your dance moves there, Ms. Fisher?

1426
01:08:53.230 --> 01:08:53.750
You can.

1427
01:08:54.390 --> 01:08:55.470
What are you going to say?

1428
01:08:56.030 --> 01:08:57.210
I've danced with you.

1429
01:08:57.510 --> 01:09:02.030
And I can tell you right now, folks, that was not a choreographed dance routine.

1430
01:09:02.290 --> 01:09:03.990
That was just Jenna being Jenna.

1431
01:09:04.230 --> 01:09:04.450
Yeah.

1432
01:09:04.630 --> 01:09:07.950
We had a fan question from Zaria Collins who asked that same question.

1433
01:09:08.170 --> 01:09:10.730
Were those dance moves choreographed?

1434
01:09:10.810 --> 01:09:11.190
Oh, no.

1435
01:09:11.410 --> 01:09:11.750
Oh, no.

1436
01:09:11.930 --> 01:09:12.950
That's all Ms. Fisher.

1437
01:09:13.310 --> 01:09:16.930
That's me fully dancing with my heart and soul.

1438
01:09:16.930 --> 01:09:18.850
That's hello, St. Louis.

1439
01:09:20.210 --> 01:09:21.410
St. Louis prom.

1440
01:09:21.870 --> 01:09:23.010
That sounds of Scranton right there.

1441
01:09:23.150 --> 01:09:27.610
That's the same girl who made a sounds of Scranton playlist, everyone.

1442
01:09:28.210 --> 01:09:29.230
There I am.

1443
01:09:29.370 --> 01:09:32.810
You could almost rewind me and put me in my high school gym right there.

1444
01:09:32.810 --> 01:09:39.430
Well, something is going to happen that is super awkward because that is Michael's way.

1445
01:09:40.370 --> 01:09:45.390
Michael's way is to take a wonderful moment and make everyone cringe.

1446
01:09:45.830 --> 01:09:48.850
And the Diwali was going to be no exception.

1447
01:09:49.570 --> 01:09:55.330
He, you know, has this amazing scene with Mindy's parents that play Kelly's parents,

1448
01:09:55.490 --> 01:09:56.490
which we already talked about.

1449
01:09:56.750 --> 01:09:59.870
And he's so inspired by their love.

1450
01:10:00.430 --> 01:10:01.570
He's going to do it.

1451
01:10:01.630 --> 01:10:01.770
Yeah.

1452
01:10:01.770 --> 01:10:02.790
He's going to do it.

1453
01:10:02.910 --> 01:10:03.530
Their commitment.

1454
01:10:03.990 --> 01:10:04.450
Yeah.

1455
01:10:04.650 --> 01:10:12.170
He's going to propose to Carol in front of a whole room of strangers on their ninth date.

1456
01:10:15.160 --> 01:10:19.340
She's like, Carol, will you do me the honor of making me your husband?

1457
01:10:19.940 --> 01:10:21.460
Of making me your husband.

1458
01:10:21.700 --> 01:10:24.960
And she's like, can we talk about this in private?

1459
01:10:25.360 --> 01:10:30.080
And this is one of my favorite moments in movies and TV where he's like, what?

1460
01:10:30.260 --> 01:10:31.060
Into a microphone.

1461
01:10:31.060 --> 01:10:34.600
And she's like, can we talk about it in private?

1462
01:10:35.980 --> 01:10:38.420
And then he's like, oh, man, oh, crap.

1463
01:10:40.200 --> 01:10:43.200
Well, they have this scene out in the parking lot, Jenna.

1464
01:10:43.200 --> 01:10:48.620
And it made me laugh so hard that, you know, Carol is like, I can't do this, Michael.

1465
01:10:48.700 --> 01:10:49.260
I can't do it.

1466
01:10:49.380 --> 01:10:56.300
And his last ditch effort, his last few moments, what is he going to say that might change her mind?

1467
01:10:56.500 --> 01:10:57.700
He's going to go for it.

1468
01:10:57.700 --> 01:11:00.800
What could he say to change this woman's mind?

1469
01:11:01.040 --> 01:11:02.060
Do you know what he says?

1470
01:11:02.220 --> 01:11:03.380
Let me come with you.

1471
01:11:03.580 --> 01:11:06.080
I have this book, the Kama Sutra.

1472
01:11:09.420 --> 01:11:12.400
She says, good night, Michael.

1473
01:11:12.400 --> 01:11:20.720
Well, at this point, Pam is, she's talking to Valley and she's realizing something.

1474
01:11:21.180 --> 01:11:23.020
She wants to reach out to Jim.

1475
01:11:23.520 --> 01:11:25.980
So she's going to, she's going to text Jim.

1476
01:11:26.080 --> 01:11:26.720
Well, that thing happened.

1477
01:11:26.980 --> 01:11:31.880
That thing happened, which is, you know, this, this crazy moment just happened.

1478
01:11:32.100 --> 01:11:33.780
And who does she want to share it with?

1479
01:11:33.960 --> 01:11:34.480
Right?

1480
01:11:35.100 --> 01:11:37.820
This is how, you know, you really care about someone.

1481
01:11:38.280 --> 01:11:43.540
Your person out there, folks, is the person you want to tell everything to right after it happens.

1482
01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:46.000
It's who you bounce everything off of.

1483
01:11:46.240 --> 01:11:49.980
And Pam wants to tell her person what just happened.

1484
01:11:51.540 --> 01:11:53.040
But she runs into Angela.

1485
01:11:54.700 --> 01:11:56.460
She needs to get her shoes.

1486
01:11:56.840 --> 01:12:00.300
And there is Angela guarding the shoes, she says.

1487
01:12:00.520 --> 01:12:02.460
Well, and eating her dry naan.

1488
01:12:02.460 --> 01:12:05.080
And by the way, Angela, fan question from Rainy Greg.

1489
01:12:05.280 --> 01:12:06.180
Was the naan dry?

1490
01:12:06.780 --> 01:12:07.180
No.

1491
01:12:07.680 --> 01:12:08.780
Was it actually dry?

1492
01:12:09.040 --> 01:12:09.360
No, it wasn't.

1493
01:12:09.500 --> 01:12:10.900
It was perfectly fine.

1494
01:12:11.200 --> 01:12:13.140
I would say that too.

1495
01:12:13.180 --> 01:12:13.880
I ate some of that naan.

1496
01:12:13.880 --> 01:12:14.400
It was wonderful.

1497
01:12:14.680 --> 01:12:15.620
I was glad to have it.

1498
01:12:15.780 --> 01:12:16.960
I was probably hungry.

1499
01:12:17.300 --> 01:12:22.700
Well, Jen and I used to always get so tickled to have scenes together because it rarely happened.

1500
01:12:23.080 --> 01:12:25.320
So we were really excited about this.

1501
01:12:25.500 --> 01:12:27.720
I loved shooting the scene with you.

1502
01:12:27.860 --> 01:12:29.100
And I love it so much.

1503
01:12:29.220 --> 01:12:30.400
I just want us to play it.

1504
01:12:30.540 --> 01:12:31.460
Sam, can you play it?

1505
01:12:32.620 --> 01:12:33.560
It's hot in there.

1506
01:12:35.400 --> 01:12:36.280
How's the naan?

1507
01:12:36.740 --> 01:12:37.060
Dry.

1508
01:12:37.960 --> 01:12:39.300
You look like you were having fun.

1509
01:12:39.880 --> 01:12:40.540
I am.

1510
01:12:40.720 --> 01:12:41.940
You should come dance with us.

1511
01:12:42.200 --> 01:12:44.460
I have to watch our shoes so they don't get stolen.

1512
01:12:45.100 --> 01:12:46.080
Who are you texting?

1513
01:12:46.500 --> 01:12:47.040
No one.

1514
01:12:48.080 --> 01:12:48.320
Aw.

1515
01:12:48.540 --> 01:12:52.720
But also, lady, my character is so nosy.

1516
01:12:53.760 --> 01:12:54.460
So nosy?

1517
01:12:54.540 --> 01:12:55.020
Who are you texting?

1518
01:12:55.020 --> 01:12:56.040
Yeah, it looked like you were having fun.

1519
01:12:56.060 --> 01:12:56.660
Who are you texting?

1520
01:12:56.660 --> 01:12:59.700
I mean, who am I to ask you who you're texting?

1521
01:13:00.760 --> 01:13:02.120
You're the party police.

1522
01:13:02.340 --> 01:13:03.860
Also, you're single.

1523
01:13:04.420 --> 01:13:06.480
Dwight made this big announcement that he's single.

1524
01:13:06.820 --> 01:13:07.440
I don't know.

1525
01:13:07.600 --> 01:13:08.700
Maybe you're texting Dwight.

1526
01:13:08.860 --> 01:13:09.420
What's happening?

1527
01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:11.360
Angela's spinning out in this episode.

1528
01:13:11.580 --> 01:13:13.520
And a lot of those scenes ended up getting deleted.

1529
01:13:13.520 --> 01:13:16.580
But it would be a fun watch to go back and watch them.

1530
01:13:16.740 --> 01:13:19.620
Because that is why you are so intense in this episode.

1531
01:13:20.060 --> 01:13:23.180
So now, Pam is going to make it outside.

1532
01:13:23.480 --> 01:13:26.380
She hasn't received a text back from Jim.

1533
01:13:26.800 --> 01:13:28.580
And she sits with Michael.

1534
01:13:29.360 --> 01:13:30.920
Michael tries to relate to her.

1535
01:13:31.060 --> 01:13:33.680
He's like, wow, they're both victims of broken engagements.

1536
01:13:33.680 --> 01:13:39.000
And Pam's like, well, I mean, except that you were never actually engaged.

1537
01:13:39.180 --> 01:13:39.740
But whatever.

1538
01:13:40.000 --> 01:13:41.700
She tries to bond with Michael.

1539
01:13:41.700 --> 01:13:48.400
And of course, he does that thing that you were just talking about where he just takes it one step too far.

1540
01:13:48.660 --> 01:13:52.380
And he starts to lean in like he's going to kiss her.

1541
01:13:52.940 --> 01:13:53.760
So awkward.

1542
01:13:54.200 --> 01:13:56.280
We got a lot of mail about it, Angela.

1543
01:13:57.420 --> 01:14:02.980
Ruby, Alexandra, and Vanessa Ortiz all wrote in to ask if that was a scripted moment.

1544
01:14:02.980 --> 01:14:07.820
When Michael tries to kiss Pam, what was it like?

1545
01:14:08.020 --> 01:14:09.920
It was scripted, you guys.

1546
01:14:10.120 --> 01:14:11.320
That was in the script.

1547
01:14:11.320 --> 01:14:17.760
And then the thing, that great line that Pam has where she says, I'm rejecting your kiss.

1548
01:14:17.920 --> 01:14:19.440
He's like, she's like, what are you doing?

1549
01:14:19.500 --> 01:14:20.220
He's like, what are you doing?

1550
01:14:20.320 --> 01:14:22.240
She's like, I'm rejecting your kiss.

1551
01:14:22.400 --> 01:14:23.340
That's what I'm doing.

1552
01:14:23.480 --> 01:14:23.680
Yeah.

1553
01:14:24.280 --> 01:14:25.500
What are you doing?

1554
01:14:25.760 --> 01:14:27.240
That was all scripted.

1555
01:14:27.240 --> 01:14:35.040
And Angela, I was so excited to do that scene because I remember staying late that evening and shooting outside.

1556
01:14:35.400 --> 01:14:42.860
I talked about this before when I had that scene with John up on the roof where Pam and Jim eat the grilled cheese sandwiches.

1557
01:14:42.860 --> 01:14:46.480
It was one of those warm summer evenings in Los Angeles.

1558
01:14:46.480 --> 01:14:47.440
They're the beSt.

1559
01:14:47.440 --> 01:14:49.540
This was another one of those.

1560
01:14:49.860 --> 01:14:57.260
And it's one of my fondest memories from shooting the show because I got Steve all to myself and I got Miguel Arteta all to myself.

1561
01:14:57.600 --> 01:15:03.260
And Mindy was there and it was just us doing the scene, getting it just perfect.

1562
01:15:03.260 --> 01:15:05.420
It felt like we had all the time in the world.

1563
01:15:05.420 --> 01:15:06.640
There was no rush.

1564
01:15:06.640 --> 01:15:09.940
And, oh, I just absolutely loved it.

1565
01:15:10.260 --> 01:15:10.360
Yeah.

1566
01:15:10.580 --> 01:15:18.320
Well, Mindy mentioned, you know, that she was kind of jealous of her parents that they got to have this great scene with Steve because there are several characters,

1567
01:15:18.580 --> 01:15:22.140
myself included, that rarely got to have one-on-one scenes with Steve.

1568
01:15:22.280 --> 01:15:24.400
It just wouldn't make sense in the world of the show.

1569
01:15:24.580 --> 01:15:28.060
And whenever I did, it felt so special.

1570
01:15:28.300 --> 01:15:33.520
And I think you got to have some amazing scenes with him throughout the course of the show.

1571
01:15:33.520 --> 01:15:40.100
And this is just one of those that was just beautiful and so fun and funny and cringy and heartfelt.

1572
01:15:40.360 --> 01:15:41.420
Just all of it.

1573
01:15:41.560 --> 01:15:42.160
That's all true.

1574
01:15:42.340 --> 01:15:47.140
Angela, we did have someone write in with an old tech alert that I thought you would appreciate.

1575
01:15:47.140 --> 01:15:47.560
Hit me up.

1576
01:15:47.600 --> 01:15:48.320
How did I miss it?

1577
01:15:48.400 --> 01:15:48.840
What is it?

1578
01:15:48.980 --> 01:15:53.640
Kayla Whitehead said Pam's cell phone is such old tech.

1579
01:15:53.760 --> 01:16:02.740
But she's like, but also when she walks outside, Michael sees her on the steps and he notices that she's holding her phone and he says, expecting a call.

1580
01:16:03.220 --> 01:16:05.640
She was like, no one would say that to you today.

1581
01:16:05.820 --> 01:16:11.800
If you have your phone in your hand today, no one's like expecting a call because we always all have our phones in our hands.

1582
01:16:11.960 --> 01:16:14.040
That is a brilliant catch.

1583
01:16:14.240 --> 01:16:16.460
I am applauding that catch.

1584
01:16:16.660 --> 01:16:17.960
I love that observation.

1585
01:16:18.400 --> 01:16:22.320
That is an amazing observation because back then, yeah, your phone was in your purse.

1586
01:16:22.480 --> 01:16:28.360
It was we didn't walk around holding phones like flip phones like that because we did hardly anything with them other than talk to someone.

1587
01:16:28.440 --> 01:16:31.920
So if you're holding it, you'd probably just spoke to someone or you were about to.

1588
01:16:31.920 --> 01:16:33.960
Yes, that is a great observation.

1589
01:16:34.220 --> 01:16:34.420
Pretty great.

1590
01:16:34.700 --> 01:16:44.820
Well, I want to take us back to Stanford because I think there is a moment in this episode that is the happiest we have seen Andy since he has appeared on the show.

1591
01:16:44.820 --> 01:16:46.640
So it's happy, Andy.

1592
01:16:47.060 --> 01:16:48.180
And I want to talk.

1593
01:16:48.520 --> 01:16:50.660
I want to share happy Andy with you.

1594
01:16:51.320 --> 01:16:53.660
Happy Andy happens at around 15 minutes.

1595
01:16:54.500 --> 01:16:56.540
They have had a lot of Jaeger.

1596
01:16:57.060 --> 01:17:01.100
Karen, though, she's just tossing her Jaeger shots into the trash.

1597
01:17:01.280 --> 01:17:02.580
No one knows it.

1598
01:17:02.580 --> 01:17:04.320
She's not getting wasted.

1599
01:17:04.940 --> 01:17:07.780
And Andy starts singing acapella.

1600
01:17:07.940 --> 01:17:09.520
Karen's like, no acapella, Andy.

1601
01:17:09.700 --> 01:17:13.680
But he's drunk and he's singing the Indigo Girls Closer to Fine.

1602
01:17:13.980 --> 01:17:20.620
And as he drunkenly sings, all of a sudden, Jim, who's super wasted, starts joining in and singing.

1603
01:17:20.940 --> 01:17:23.420
And it's so adorable.

1604
01:17:23.680 --> 01:17:25.100
Andy's like, Tuna!

1605
01:17:25.100 --> 01:17:26.240
Are you kidding?

1606
01:17:28.100 --> 01:17:30.220
He is so happy.

1607
01:17:30.540 --> 01:17:31.520
He's so happy.

1608
01:17:31.640 --> 01:17:33.500
They're having like an acapella moment.

1609
01:17:33.800 --> 01:17:35.660
And this is happy Andy.

1610
01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:36.700
He is thrilled.

1611
01:17:37.120 --> 01:17:41.740
Well, Angela, we had a fan catch for Renata Torres.

1612
01:17:42.360 --> 01:17:49.700
She says at 17 minutes, 58 seconds, you can see a pair of white flip flops under Karen's desk.

1613
01:17:50.260 --> 01:17:52.740
And she wanted to know if that was on purpose.

1614
01:17:52.740 --> 01:17:54.560
But we know why those are there.

1615
01:17:54.780 --> 01:17:55.460
We do.

1616
01:17:55.660 --> 01:17:57.160
Those were Rashida's flip flops.

1617
01:17:57.160 --> 01:18:04.760
Yeah, the wardrobe department would give us Uggs or flip flops to wear to and from our trailers and set.

1618
01:18:04.880 --> 01:18:09.420
So we didn't have to walk in our kind of like high heel office shoes, right?

1619
01:18:09.620 --> 01:18:09.840
Yeah.

1620
01:18:10.660 --> 01:18:11.140
Yes.

1621
01:18:11.380 --> 01:18:14.300
You caught Rashida's flip flops.

1622
01:18:14.480 --> 01:18:20.460
You know, wardrobe actually told me one time also, our trailers were not close to the soundstage.

1623
01:18:20.640 --> 01:18:22.140
It was a little, you know, quite a walk.

1624
01:18:22.140 --> 01:18:31.460
And they said that also they would take our shoes to protect our shoes because if we walked across the parking lot back and forth and sometimes if there was weather of any kind,

1625
01:18:31.740 --> 01:18:39.480
they preferred actually to leave our shoes on set by our desks rather than us walking around in them all the time.

1626
01:18:39.480 --> 01:18:41.980
And we were delighted because that meant less time in heels.

1627
01:18:42.200 --> 01:18:43.580
We had our travel shoes.

1628
01:18:43.840 --> 01:18:45.760
Those were Rashida's travel shoes.

1629
01:18:46.460 --> 01:18:52.360
Well, as they're leaving for the night in Stanford, Jim is going to ride that bike home.

1630
01:18:52.540 --> 01:18:54.120
He's going to ride his bike home.

1631
01:18:54.280 --> 01:18:55.200
Or is he?

1632
01:18:55.340 --> 01:18:55.880
Well, yeah.

1633
01:18:56.080 --> 01:18:57.080
He falls over.

1634
01:18:57.320 --> 01:18:59.380
Well, you know, it's the end of the night at Stanford.

1635
01:18:59.380 --> 01:19:00.340
They've had Jaeger.

1636
01:19:00.340 --> 01:19:02.400
They've bonded over indigo girls.

1637
01:19:02.900 --> 01:19:05.440
I mean, Andy's busting out his air mattress.

1638
01:19:05.820 --> 01:19:06.420
He's like.

1639
01:19:06.660 --> 01:19:07.080
Oh, yeah.

1640
01:19:07.300 --> 01:19:08.980
He's staying in for the night.

1641
01:19:09.520 --> 01:19:13.520
Jim is going to try to ride his giant bicycle with the big basket home.

1642
01:19:13.720 --> 01:19:18.920
And he like tips over into the bushes and Karen's in her car.

1643
01:19:19.080 --> 01:19:20.040
She's like, hold up.

1644
01:19:20.200 --> 01:19:21.020
Get in my car.

1645
01:19:21.200 --> 01:19:21.460
Drunky.

1646
01:19:22.260 --> 01:19:26.420
And Jenna, do you remember how freaked out people were about this moment?

1647
01:19:27.720 --> 01:19:28.240
Yeah.

1648
01:19:28.240 --> 01:19:34.800
I mean, people thought Karen was shady, that she let them get so wasted, and that was she

1649
01:19:34.800 --> 01:19:35.640
waiting for Jim?

1650
01:19:35.660 --> 01:19:37.040
Like she had planned it all along.

1651
01:19:37.040 --> 01:19:37.180
Yeah.

1652
01:19:37.180 --> 01:19:39.240
Was she waiting out in the parking lot for Jim?

1653
01:19:39.240 --> 01:19:41.520
I was like, hey, Mr. Tipsy, get in my car.

1654
01:19:41.800 --> 01:19:46.560
And remember, in this episode, it was written that they were going to like kiss.

1655
01:19:46.620 --> 01:19:48.420
Oh, I talked to Rashida about it.

1656
01:19:48.480 --> 01:19:52.120
I texted with her, and I want to read you guys what she said.

1657
01:19:52.280 --> 01:19:57.800
She said, in this episode, they had written a scene where Jim and Karen get sloppy drunk

1658
01:19:57.800 --> 01:19:58.980
and make out.

1659
01:19:59.220 --> 01:20:03.160
So maybe, I guess, she had been drinking too in that different version, right?

1660
01:20:03.740 --> 01:20:09.360
In that different version, because I have the scripted version of that, the three of them go to

1661
01:20:09.360 --> 01:20:12.580
a bar, and they all get drunk together at a bar.

1662
01:20:12.780 --> 01:20:16.680
And then they were supposed to make out on the street outside of this bar.

1663
01:20:16.680 --> 01:20:16.940
Yeah.

1664
01:20:17.260 --> 01:20:22.160
And Rashida said they actually filmed the scene in the parking lot.

1665
01:20:23.100 --> 01:20:24.180
Oh, my God.

1666
01:20:24.500 --> 01:20:26.500
And she said she was really worried.

1667
01:20:26.640 --> 01:20:27.780
She was like, everyone's going to hate me.

1668
01:20:27.960 --> 01:20:33.040
And then she told me Stephen Merchant actually suggested that they cut the scene out.

1669
01:20:33.320 --> 01:20:33.640
Huh.

1670
01:20:33.940 --> 01:20:35.360
That he got to watch a verse.

1671
01:20:35.480 --> 01:20:40.360
Because Stephen and Ricky would watch our episodes, and they would give the producers notes.

1672
01:20:40.900 --> 01:20:42.200
Rarely, but sometimes.

1673
01:20:42.200 --> 01:20:44.800
And their notes were always correct.

1674
01:20:45.140 --> 01:20:48.380
They were always like, they knew, don't move that needle so far.

1675
01:20:48.580 --> 01:20:48.660
Yeah.

1676
01:20:48.860 --> 01:20:54.400
And Rashida said she felt like Stephen really understood the relationships, and that this

